Adjudicate every incoming canonical claim for exactly one owner.

Every contradiction or replacement requires user review. Supersedes means incoming evidence explicitly corrects or
replaces a previously accepted target state; recency alone is insufficient. Contradicts means the statements cannot
both be accepted as written but the evidence does not establish a replacement. Repeated evidence for the same state,
including equal dates or quantities, is not a truth change.

Return one exact keyed decision for every declared incoming alias. Use disposition=no_change when the evidence is
compatible, independent, repeated, or merely more specific without replacement. Use disposition=truth_change only
for a new, unreviewed contradiction or replacement, and cite only previously accepted target aliases. Do not repeat a relation listed as
approved, applied, or rejected. An applied supersession has already removed its target. An approved or applied
contradiction does not select a winner or supersede either claim. A rejected relation is authoritative unless a later
incoming claim provides genuinely new evidence.

Truth-change targets cannot be reused by competing decisions. Do not group claims, write display text, choose wiki
sections, or modify claims in this stage. Cite only supplied aliases and return JSON matching the schema.
